            "review_title": "Review at Soi10 Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jennie D\nHanoi, Vietnam119 contributions\n0\nNot good food, bad service\nJan 2016 • Friends\nOrdered:\n- Papaya salad: not even close to Thai papaya salad..both appearance wise n taste\n- Stir-fried kang kong: ok, not so bad\n- Beef larb: best dish out of the whole meal\n- Grilled fish: ok\n- Roasted shrimps with glass noodles in hotpot: super salty\n- Crab fried rice: not bad\n- Pineapple fried rice: too soggy \n\nService: horrible!! I called in advance to order the food. I asked if they have the crab fried rice and the manager said they don't have it today. When we were at the restaurant, one of my colleagues asked if there's pineapple fried rice..the waiter said there is only 1 left, in my defense we were the only ppl in the restaurant. Later I asked if there's different kind of fried rice, the waiter said \"crab fried rice\" (on the fone they said No). So I asked her to ask how many portions of crab fried rice n pineapple fried rice available. She came back and told me 2 of each., I specifically said 2 pineapple and 1 crab. Then she brought out 2 crab n 1 pineapple!!! And she said theres only 1 pineapple left!!! Seriously what is wrong with the service at this restaurant?!?! \n\nNot recommend this place n wouldn't come back here again\nRead more\nWritten January 19, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
