            "review_title": "Review at Soi10 Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tony N\nHanoi, Vietnam63 contributions\n0\nAwesome Thai seafood' Restaurant in Hanoi\nAug 2015 • Solo\nThe restaurant located in the centre of district. I was there for dining after business meeting. In the begining, the hostest welcome me at the entrance and show off the menu with so many traditional Thai cuisine. I found out my flavour one Thai tom yum soup so i decided to check in. I am willing to stay at second floor, the waiter taking my order just 5 mins later i got it. So...good...so yummy 100% the flavour and spices of tom yum soup made by executive chef from Thailand and such a reasonable price @ 75.000 VND only. Moreover, It's beyond my expectation i can't believe that i have chance to enjoy the original taste of Thai cuisine in Hanoi. Excellent customer service, kindly and helpful staff thank to right vision and management style in hospitality as well. There are so many Thai Restaurants in Hanoi but i prefer you this is the original one for Thai cuisine lover like me. For sure, i will be back and pick it up for my son - his very first one birthday party at the end of this month. Thank you for taking care of me. Keep it up.\nRead more\nWritten August 16, 2015",
